      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2144745026,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> This is necessary to ensure that these application modal dialogs stay always on top on Linux.\n\nAnd other platforms using X11 or Wayland as the underlying window system, presumably.\n\nIt may also result in message boxes using the native message box (or in Qt doing a better job of emulating the native message box) on macOS - I noticed that newer versions of Wireshark have message boxes that don't look weird on macOS.",
